{"id":14139,"volId":745,"name":"Star of the county down","artist":"Celtas Cortos","album":"Introversiones","cover":"http://img-cdn2.luoo.net/pics/albums/8332/cover.jpg","url":"http://mp3-cdn2.luoo.net/low/luoo/radio727/01.mp3","color":"#3d436b","lyric":"[by:warmplayer]\n[ti:Star of the county down]\n[ar:Celtas Cortos]\n[al:Introversiones]\n[by:warmplayer]\n[00:11.20]Near banbridge town in the county down\n[00:13.66]One morning last july,\n[00:16.38]From a boreen green came a sweet colleen\n[00:19.01]And she smiled as she passed me by.\n[00:21.70]She looked so sweet from her two bare feet\n[00:24.35]To the sheen of her nut brown hair.\n[00:26.85]Such a coaxing elf, sure I shook myself\n[00:29.57]For to see I was really there.\n[00:31.69]Chorus\n[00:32.16]From bantry bay up to derry quay and\n[00:35.04]From galway to dublin town,\n[00:37.74]No maid I've seen like the brown colleen\n[00:40.35]That I met in the county down.\n[01:04.08]As she onward sped, sure I scratched my head,\n[01:07.09]And I looked with a feelin' rare,\n[01:09.76]And I say's, say's i, to a passer-by,\n[01:12.32]\"whose the maid with the nut brown hair\"? “\n[01:14.93]He smiled at me and he says's, say's he,\n[01:17.70]\"that's the gem of ireland's crown. “\n[01:20.44]It's rosie mccann from the banks of the bann,\n[01:23.07]She's the star of the county down\".\n[01:25.23]Chorus\n[01:25.50]From bantry bay up to derry ouay and\n[01:28.55]From galway to dublin town,\n[01:31.01]No maid I've seen like the brown colleen\n[01:33.49]That I met in the county down.\n[01:41.69]At the harvest fair she'll be surely there\n[01:44.22]And I'll dress in my sunday clothes,\n[01:47.12]With my shoes shone bright and my hat cocked\n[01:49.45]Right for a smile from my nut brown rose.\n[01:52.54]No pipe I'll smoke, no horse I'll yoke\n[01:54.89]Till my plough turns rust coloured brown.\n[01:57.79]Till a smiling bride, by my own fireside\n[02:00.34]Sits the star of the county down.\n[02:03.05]From bantry bay up to derry ouay and\n[02:05.90]From galway to dublin town,\n[02:08.40]No maid I've seen like the brown colleen\n[02:10.94]That I met in the county down.\n[02:13.72]From bantry bay up to derry ouay and\n[02:16.61]From galway to dublin town,\n[02:19.07]No maid I've seen like the brown colleen\n[02:21.54]That I met in the county down.\n[02:24.46]From bantry bay up to derry ouay and\n[02:27.25]From galway to dublin town,\n[02:29.69]No maid I've seen like the brown colleen\n[02:34.90]That I met in the county down.\n[03:15.95]\n","_id":"0CFcaMIwZmjh7RU3"}
