{"id":10667,"volId":514,"name":"The Town I Loved So Well","artist":"The Dubliners","album":"The Very Best of Dubliners","cover":"http://img-cdn2.luoo.net/pics/albums/5659/cover.jpg","url":"http://mp3-cdn2.luoo.net/low/luoo/radio548/10.mp3","color":"#38322c","lyric":"[ti:]The Town I Loved So Well\r\n[ar:]The Celtic Tenors\r\n[al:]Irish Album\r\n[by:]韩霄\r\n\r\n[00:01.00]The Town I Loved So Well\r\n[00:05.00]LRC歌词编辑：韩霄 HI.BAIDU.COM/ENDERVICTORKING\r\n[00:10.24]\r\n[00:16.65]In my memory I will always see\r\n[00:23.50]The town that I have loved so well\r\n[00:31.15]Where our school played ball by the gasyard wall\r\n[00:38.65]And we laughed through the smoke and the smell\r\n[00:44.00]\r\n[00:44.75]Going home in the rain, running up the dark lane\r\n[00:51.76]Past the jail and down behind the fountain\r\n[00:59.43]Those were happy days in so many, many ways\r\n[01:06.47]In the town I loved so well\r\n[01:13.00]\r\n[01:13.73]There was music there in the Derry air\r\n[01:22.26]Like a language that we all could under stand\r\n[01:28.85]I remember the day when I earned my first pay\r\n[01:36.17]And I played in a small pickup band\r\n[01:43.00]\r\n[01:44.54]There I spent my youth and to tell you the truth\r\n[01:51.43]I was sad to leave it all behind me\r\n[01:58.61]For I learned about life and I'd found a wife\r\n[02:05.81]In the town I loved so well\r\n[02:11.00]\r\n[02:12.91]But when I returned how my eyes have burned\r\n[02:19.97]To see how a town could be brought to its knees\r\n[02:26.05]By the armoured cars and the bombed out bars\r\n[02:33.73]And the gas that hangs on to every tree\r\n[02:40.72]\r\n[02:41.98]Now the army's in stalled by that old gasyard wall\r\n[02:48.83]And the damned barbed wire gets higher and higher\r\n[02:56.77]With their tanks and their guns, oh my God, what have they done\r\n[03:03.02]To the town I loved so well\r\n[03:11.00]\r\n[03:12.70]Now the music's gone but they carry on\r\n[03:21.24]For their spirit's been bruised, never broken\r\n[03:31.12]They will not for get but their hearts are set\r\n[03:39.11]On to morrow and peace once again\r\n[03:46.04]\r\n[03:48.35]For what's done is done and what's won is won\r\n[03:54.97]And what's lost is lost and gone forever\r\n[04:03.65]I can only pray for a bright, brand new day\r\n[04:11.06]In the town I loved so well\r\n[04:20.31]In the town I loved so well\r\n[04:25.73]\r\n[04:30.00]歌词编辑：韩霄\n","_id":"59W7dxS5B14ETWuY"}
