{"id":2352,"volId":339,"name":"Vincent","artist":"Don McLean","album":"Legendary Don McLean","cover":"http://img-cdn2.luoo.net/pics/albums/2091/cover.jpg","url":"http://mp3-cdn2.luoo.net/low/luoo/radio211/07.mp3","color":"","lyric":"[00:00.000]Starry starry night\n[00:04.670]paint your palette blue and grey\n[00:09.620]look out on a summer's day\n[00:12.810]with eyes that know the darkness in my soul.\n[00:17.040]Shadows on the hills\n[00:21.410]sketch the trees and the daffodils\n[00:26.440]catch the breeze and the winter chills\n[00:30.230]in colors on the snowy linen land.\n[00:36.720]And now I understand\n[00:41.210]what you tried to say to me\n[00:45.940]and how you suffered for your sanity\n[00:50.770]and how you tried to set them free.\n[00:53.820]They would not listen they did not know how\n[00:59.320]perhaps they'll listen now.\n[01:04.990]Starry starry night\n[01:09.640]flaming flowers that brightly blaze\n[01:14.880]swirling clouds in violet haze\n[01:18.550]reflect in Vincent's eyes of China blue.\n[01:22.910]Colors changing hue\n[01:27.410]morning fields of amber grain\n[01:32.620]weathered faces lined in pain\n[01:36.720]are smoothed beneath the artist's loving hand.\n[01:40.990]And now I understand\n[01:45.840]what you tried to say to me\n[01:49.710]and how you suffered for your sanity\n[01:55.040]and how you tried to set them free.\n[01:57.810]They would not listen they did not know how\n[02:03.140]perhaps they'll listen now.\n[02:06.650]For they could not love you\n[02:10.960]but still your love was true\n[02:15.780]and when no hope was left in sight on that\n[02:20.160]starry starry night.\n[02:22.640]You took your life as lovers often do'\n[02:27.720]But I could have told you Vincent\n[02:31.820]this world was never meant for one as beautiful as you.\n[02:41.130]Starry starry night\n[02:45.770]portraits hung in empty halls\n[02:50.890]frameless heads on nameless walls\n[02:54.700]with eyes that watch the world and can't forget.\n[02:58.580]Like the stranger that you've met\n[03:03.340]the ragged men in ragged clothes\n[03:07.880]the silver thorn of bloddy rose\n[03:11.380]lie crushed and broken on the virgin snow.\n[03:16.820]And now I think I know\n[03:21.770]what you tried to say to me\n[03:26.310]and how you suffered for your sanity\n[03:31.870]and how you tried to set them free.\n[03:34.690]They would not listen they're not listening still\n[03:40.680]perhaps they never will.\n","_id":"5Gc2Ll2qJg9EdH36"}
