e latest jam\n[01:42.129]But when it got shot up\n[01:43.301]They went home and said \"Damn\n[01:44.959]There's got to be a better way\n[01:46.108]To hear our music every day\n[01:47.544]B-boys getting blown away\n[01:48.583]But coming outside anyway\"\n[01:50.259]They tried again outside in Cedar Park\n[01:52.513]Power from a street light made the place dark\n[01:54.902]But yo, they didn't care, they turned it out\n[01:57.249]I know a few understand what I'm talking about\n[01:59.714]Remember Bronx River, rolling thick\n[02:02.179]With Kool DJ Red Alert\n[02:03.498]And Chuck Chillout on the mix\n[02:04.959]When Afrika Islam was rocking the jams\n[02:07.248]And on the other side of town\n[02:08.517]Was a kid named Flash\n[02:10.141]Patterson and Millbrook projects\n[02:12.266]Casanova all over, ya couldn't stop it\n[02:15.050]The Nine Lives Crew, the Cypress Boys\n[02:17.475]The real Rock Steady taking out these toys\n[02:19.854]As odd as it looked, as wild as it seems\n[02:22.203]I didn't hear a peep from a place called Queens\n[02:24.812]It was seventy-six to 1980\n[02:27.508]The dreads in Brooklyn was crazy\n[02:29.822]You couldn't bring out your set with no hip-hop\n[02:32.291]Because the pistols would go\n[02:34.787]So why don't you wise up\n[02:36.331]Show all the people in the place\n[02:38.039]That you are wack\n[02:40.460]Instead of tryna take out LL\n[02:42.235]You need to take your homeboys off the crack\n[02:45.496]Cause if you don't, well\n[02:46.920]Then their nerves will become shot\n[02:50.535]And that would leave the job up\n[02:52.616]To my own Scott La Rock and he's from\n[02:55.240]South Bronx, the South South Bronx (4x)\n[03:05.148]South Bronx, the South South Bronx (4x)\n[03:16.143]\n[04:40.543]The human TR-808, D-Nice\n[04:46.253]The poet, the Blastmaster KRS-ONE\n[04:52.201]The Grand Incredible DJ Scott La Rock\n[04:57.920]Boogie... Down... Productions\n[05:02.040]Fresh for '86, you suckers!\n","_id":"7qpalzX8dTtoiam8"}
