 my dream\n[01:50.69]That ends abruptly when they try to hug me through the screen\n[01:53.21]Of smoke that's engulfing me\n[01:55.16]Like the coastline with it's high tide\n[01:57.05]And you can see the sands and the oceans meet\n[01:59.62]No one told me when this ride began to hold my seat\n[02:02.00]Time flies like Emmet Brown was in the driver's seat\n[02:04.69]You talk of irony\n[02:06.37]Well now I'm lonely\n[02:07.19]But I'm searching for my privacy\n[02:08.31]This life won't comply with me\n[02:10.08]I think I need some dead relatives either side of me\n[02:12.76]To keep me company and guide me through the library\n[02:15.21]Of neverending stories full of lies and deceit\n[02:17.65]Hi Ho Silver, Lone Ranger riding to the beat\n[02:21.44]'Cause everything is different now\n[02:25.70]I'd really like to tell you how\n[02:31.11]How I wanted you here by my side\n[02:39.30]I know what I said but I lied\n[02:44.59]It looked like I laughed but I cried\n[02:49.71]But I wish I could push rewind\n[02:53.48]If I could rewind time to it's slowest\n[02:55.69]I'd look at life at it's heights and it's lowest\n[02:58.43]So I could maybe try to recollect\n[03:00.74]What made me who I am besides a poet\n[03:02.58]Besides a poet\n[03:06.73]How I wanted you here by my side\n[03:14.30]I know what I said but I lied\n[03:20.13]It looked like I laughed but I cried\n[03:25.10]But I wish I could push rewind\n","_id":"OeqZ5UgwUR0496S3"}
