{"id":10293,"volId":498,"name":"Blue &amp; Green","artist":"Little Hands of Asphalt","album":"Spit Back at the Rain","cover":"http://img-cdn2.luoo.net/pics/albums/5371/cover.jpg","url":"http://mp3-cdn2.luoo.net/low/luoo/radio530/02.mp3","color":"#9fb08e","lyric":"[ti:blue and green]\r\n[ar:the little hands of asphalt]\r\n[al:]\r\n[by:夏悸]\r\n[00:02.15]I got your name on a note from a friend of mine.\r\n[00:08.18]She said &quot;you guys should hang out&quot;.\r\n[00:12.18]I don't know where she gets all her bad ideas,\r\n[00:15.94]but that's how it turned out.\r\n[00:18.59]And we went up to the dam,\r\n[00:23.85]where we talked about what certain boys would be thinking.\r\n[00:27.09]It's where this city gets its' water supply.\r\n[00:31.83]But that's not what we're drinking.\r\n[00:36.40]Are you always going to change your mind?\r\n[00:46.07]\r\n[00:49.69]Somewhere in the dim the wind is stark.\r\n[00:53.66]Down there the traffic is roaring.\r\n[01:01.61]We exchanged some wasteful and stale remarks on people\r\n[01:02.33]we think are boring.\r\n[01:05.38]Then you said something 'bout caffeine and nightmares.\r\n[01:09.33]It wasn't really that elegant.\r\n[01:14.25]So the conversation got slow but we didn't care.\r\n[01:17.24]Sometimes that's insignificant.\r\n[01:31.88]Are you always going to change your mind?\r\n[01:43.24]\r\n[01:46.58]Well, I'm glad we went for a walk,\r\n[01:49.62]but it's getting late.\r\n[01:50.58]And no, I don't want to talk.\r\n[01:58.17]Let the past two years become outlines in white chalk.\r\n[02:01.67]In my room I've got this strange machine,\r\n[02:05.67]it doesn't kill fascists,\r\n[02:23.76]but it has a screen that displays my love and some coded dreams in blue and green.\r\n[02:30.64]Are you always going to change your mind?\r\n[02:37.89]Have You lost your track of time?\r\nAre you always going to change your mind?\n","_id":"dX2JWAlgN4O91d2W"}
