ot saline, Botox\n[01:29.99]Eighteen, fake tits, nineteen, detox\n[01:32.71]Don't stop, get it, get it, can't afford it? Get it credit\n[01:35.58]Buy it, spend it, try it, getting fat? Then you better shed it\n[01:38.44]Ab Swing, Blublocker, 2Pac or Biggie\n[01:41.12]East coast, West coast, Fat Joe or 50\n[01:44.01]Thatcher the shifty Iron Lady, Tony Blair\n[01:46.85]A princess died, some say cause she got Dodi there\n[01:49.71]Whitlam, Keating, Hawke and a promise\n[01:52.39]of no children in poverty, wish that could have been honest\n[01:54.86]We had Abbot and Costello, right wing overlords\n[01:57.87]Promises and children, they threw 'em both overboard\n[02:00.87]Overwrought refugees thrown to a group home\n[02:04.02]or jailed for the crime of looking for a new home\n[02:06.66]Elvis died, Hendrix died, Lennon died, genocide\n[02:09.45]In Africa, Serbia, Cambodia, pesticides\n[02:12.28]Bio-toxins, chemical warfare\n[02:15.13]All's fair in love and war, more work for the pallbearer\n[02:17.98]More terror, more unjust search and seizures\n[02:20.76]A tidal wave came and claimed the coast of Indonesia\n[02:23.56]Quakes in Iran, Japan and California\n[02:26.35]Greenhouse gas turned the world into a sauna\n[02:29.17]The trauma of mortars, martyrs, slaughters\n[02:31.98]of partners, mourners, fathers and daughters\n[02:34.79]They chased us, caught us, numbered us to sort us\n[02:37.56]Raped us, scorned us, to break us they bought us\n[02:40.46]third world kidneys for captains of industry\n[02:43.22]Uprising in the street, corruption in the ministry\n[02:46.06]A blowjob brought about the fall of a dynasty\n[02:48.82]And MP3s saw the fall of an industry\n[02:51.87]Doubled population, halved accommodation\n[02:54.56]Carved up resources and we starved the poorer nations\n[02:57.46]Beirut, Chechnya, all hell broke loose\n[03:00.27]Berlin, nineteen-eighty-nine man, the wall fell\n[03:03.22]Cold war ended but that didn't stop more shells\n[03:05.98]Waco lit up the sky like burning oil wells\n[03:08.81]A world laid waste with addiction\n[03:11.42]Tell Orwell truth's always stranger than fiction\n[03:14.26]Big Brother's on closed circuit TV and on cable\n[03:16.94]Reality's now scripted, celebrities for sale\n[03:19.79]Jeopardy and jail, seized, deposed\n[03:22.76]Remedies and penalties for failed CEOs\n[03:24.30]We had the Enron collapse and white-collar crime\n[03:28.54]Investors they were taxed, a dollar for a dime\n[03:31.28]The blue chip companies and blue-sky mines\n[03:33.96]We no longer choose sides we choose sidelines\n[03:36.91]Rich bleeding the kind, blind leading the blind\n[03:39.51]And history repeats, no competing with time\n[03:42.42]Gasses eating the minds of the vets that they bring home\n[03:45.61]The plague of Agent Orange, Gulf War syndrome\n[03:48.37]Soldiers sent home, posttraumatic stress leave\n[03:51.22]STDs cause the sleeve ain't sexy\n[03:53.99]AIDS shook the eighties, grim reaper with a bowling ball\n[03:56.90]Metallica \"Kill 'Em All\", let God scold 'em all\n[03:59.56]The Guildford Four, Chicago Seven\n[04:02.30]Mumia, Mandela, Ocean's Eleven\n[04:05.10]Half past twelve on Friday the Thirteenth\n[04:08.12]Dawn of the Dead, A Nightmare on Elm Street\n[04:10.93]Weapons free environment, war zone, phone home\n[04:13.75]Melanoma grow as we soak in the ozone\n[04:15.91]Home-grown, Hydro, Cocaine, Nitro\n[04:19.46]Werewolf in London, American Psycho\n[04:22.21]Check, cyclones, bushfires, Bush firing scuds\n[04:25.09]Baby boomers, Woodstock, what happened to the love?\n[04:27.85]What happened to the cubs? They fed 'em to the wolves\n[04:30.62]Set a trial for paedophiles, they let 'em in the schools\n[04:33.50]Set 'em on the students, turned 'em on the kids\n[04:36.20]And everyone responsible should burn for what they did\n[04:39.17]And if they try to deny then an eye for an eye\n[04:42.06]The government and church on which we try to rely\n[04:44.90]both rob us till it hurts chasing lie after lie\n[04:47.56]like astr